# SEL: the common page (engine, volume, send 1, send 2); the LFO is for synths only; the scatter row has 1/8
expect view 0
tap SEL
expect view 7
shot common.png
# track 1 (KICK W, engine 1): volume and the two sends (they start at 0)
expect eng 1
turn K2 -5
expectlevel 0 90
expectsend 0 0 0
expectsend 1 0 0
turn K3 10
expectsend 0 0 20
turn K4 5
expectsend 1 0 10
# another track keeps its own
tapkey b2
expectsend 1 2 0
expectlevel 2 100
# the engine: K1 steps through the list (track 3 starts on 909 CH = 9)
turn K1 1
expect eng 11
# SEL again goes back to the sequencer
tap SEL
expect view 0
# the LFO: not on drums, yes on the 303
tap LFO
expect view 0
tapkey b5
tap LFO
expect view 1
expect grp 2
# the kick P has no click page entries: its ENV page lists Dur, SwpShp, SwpDpt, FMSnap
tapkey b6
tap ENV
shot kickp_env.png
